PROBLEM DESCRIPTION You are given N rooms (1 <= N <= 10^5) and an array litres of length N, where litres[i] is the number of litres of paint required to paint the i-th room. All required paint is pooled together, so you need at least T = sum(litres[i]) litres in total. 
You can buy paint any number of times from two pack options: 
•	Single pack: costs a and provides 1 litre of paint.
•	Bulk pack: costs b and provides S litres of paint.
You may buy more litres than strictly needed if a bulk pack is cheaper overall. Find the minimum total cost required to obtain at least T litres of paint. 
INPUT FORMAT First line contains four integers N, a, b, and S. Second line contains N space-separated integers representing the array litres. 
OUTPUT FORMAT Print a single integer representing the minimum total cost. 



public class Main {

    public static void main(String[] args) {

        int N = 3;
        int a = 5;
        int b = 8;
        int S = 5;

        int[] litres = {2, 3, 2};

        long T = 0;

        for (int i = 0; i < N; i++) {
            T += litres[i];
        }

        long cost1 = T * a;

        long cost2 = (T / S) * b + (T % S) * a;

        long bulkPacks = (T + S - 1) / S;

        long cost3 = bulkPacks * b;

        long answer = Math.min(cost1, Math.min(cost2, cost3));

        System.out.println(answer);
    }
}
